2794354222714901, 0.035727985203266144, 0.02945784106850624, 0.01718965545296669, 0.014066414907574654, 0.021957330405712128, 0.003359850263223052, -0.004776547662913799, -0.0021605375222861767, -0.013261944055557251, 0.03118508867919445, -0.00976012833416462, -0.012575777247548103, -0.01125076599419117, 0.017154164612293243, -0.01334475725889206, 0.03639049082994461, -0.03066454827785492, 0.04822094738483429, 0.022726310417056084, -0.0157463401556015, 0.0052497657015919685, -0.023921186104416847, -0.008405541069805622, 0.023294173181056976, -0.005974381696432829, 0.010777547955513, 0.019745035097002983, 0.014681599102914333, 0.0637425109744072, -0.06700771301984787, -0.009937585331499577, 0.0500665009021759, -0.009718721732497215, -0.0032888674177229404, 0.017639214172959328, 0.01123893540352583, 0.017674705013632774, 0.011605679988861084, -0.03833068534731865, -0.018479175865650177, -0.018372701480984688, -0.01807694137096405, -0.009523519314825535, -0.008807776495814323, 0.007926407270133495, 0.0205613374710083, -0.006258312612771988, 0.009215926751494408]], "input": ["CARMEN RIBES KONINCKX:Carmen Ribes Koninckx is the head of the Pediatrics section, focusing on the Digestive System.", "CAROLINA FUENTES SOCORRO:Carolina Fuentes Socorro is a specialist in Pediatrics, focusing on Pediatric Oncology.", "RAMON SANCHIS RAMADA:Ramon Sanchis Ramada is a specialist in Pediatrics, focusing on Pediatric Intensive Care.", "CARLOS GUTIERREZ SAN ROMAN:Carlos Gutierrez San Roman is the head of the Pediatrics section, focusing on General Surgery.", "MANUAL DE NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL:The \"Manual de Nutrición Artificial\" is a clinical guide designed to enhance nutritional practices within healthcare settings. It serves as a resource for healthcare professionals to improve the quality of nutritional care provided to patients.", "DEPARTAMENTO DE SALUD VALENCIA(\"ENTITY\":", "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:The European Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ESPEN) is an organization dedicated to advancing research and education in the field of parenteral and enteral nutrition throughout Europe. Its primary focus is on enhancing the quality of nutritional care for patients who require these forms of nutrition. ESPEN plays a crucial role in improving clinical practices by providing guidelines and recommendations that inform healthcare professionals on best practices in nutritional care. Through its efforts, ESPEN aims to support the overall improvement of nutritional practices and outcomes for patients across the continent.", "NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL:\"NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL\" refers to a medical intervention that provides nutritional support to patients who are unable to consume food orally. This method is crucial for individuals with severe dietary restrictions, swallowing difficulties, or specific medical conditions such as liver diseases, celiac disease, and various forms of cancer. Nutritional support can be delivered through enteral or parenteral means, depending on the patient's condition and needs.\n\nThe practice of artificial nutrition is particularly relevant in critical care settings and for patients suffering from malnutrition, metabolic disorders, or those requiring mechanical ventilation due to severe burns. It is also indicated for patients with inflammatory bowel diseases and those experiencing complications like hyponatremia or diabetes, especially in cases such as MELAS syndrome.\n\nArtificial nutrition aims to prevent malnutrition and restore nutritional status, utilizing specialized formulas to correct deficiencies. It is a therapeutic approach that may be palliative and is not considered basic care, as its application depends on the individual circumstances of each patient. Overall, \"NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL\" encompasses a range of nutritional support methods designed to meet the needs of patients who cannot achieve adequate nutrition through normal eating.", "PACIENTE QUIRÚRGICO:The \"PACIENTE QUIRÚRGICO\" refers to an individual who is undergoing a surgical procedure. This type of patient may benefit from specific nutritional formulas designed to enhance their recovery process. Specialized nutritional support is often necessary for these patients to ensure optimal healing and overall health following surgery.", "POLITRAUMATISMOS:Politraumatismos refer to multiple traumatic injuries occurring simultaneously, which often necessitate complex medical management. These injuries can lead to significant challenges in patient care, including the potential need for enteral nutrition due to the inability to ingest food normally. Consequently, patients with politraumatismos may require nutritional support as part of their recovery process, highlighting the importance of comprehensive treatment strategies in managing such complex cases.", "SEPSIS:Sepsis is a life-threatening condition that arises from the body's extreme response to infection, leading to significant injury to its own tissues and organs. It is particularly prevalent among critically ill patients and can complicate the treatment of those requiring parenteral nutrition. The condition is characterized by systemic inflammation, which can result in elevated liver enzymes and increased energy expenditure, especially in pediatric patients. \n\nSepsis can develop in various clinical contexts, including patients with short bowel syndrome, those receiving nutritional support, and individuals suffering from acute pancreatitis. It is often associated with catheter-related infections, which can significantly increase morbidity. The condition can also influence nutritional needs, potentially leading to insufficient nutrient intake and necessitating enteral nutrition. \n\nIn managing sepsis, specific nutritional interventions, including amino acid supplementation, may be beneficial to support recovery and address the heightened metabolic stress experienced by affected patients. Overall, sepsis represents a serious medical challenge that requires urgent treatment and specialized nutritional care to improve patient outcomes.", "INSUFICIENCIA RESPIRATORIA:Insuficiencia respiratoria, or respiratory failure, is a medical condition characterized by the inability to maintain adequate gas exchange, leading to insufficient oxygen supply and/or carbon dioxide removal from the body. This condition often necessitates specialized nutritional support for affected patients, as they may experience poor fluid management and require specific nutritional formulations to aid in their recovery. Insuficiencia respiratoria can occur in patients with progressive muscle weakness, such as those suffering from Kennedy's syndrome, which further complicates their ability to breathe effectively.", "INSUFICIENCIA RENAL:\"Insuficiencia renal,\" or renal insufficiency, is a medical condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to effectively filter waste products from the blood. This condition can lead to significant health complications, including malnutrition and the need for specialized dietary adjustments. Patients with insuficiencia renal often require tailored nutritional support to manage their health, as the condition can affect protein levels, fluid and electrolyte needs, and overall nutritional status.\n\nThe condition may necessitate the use of specific nutritional products, such as Nepro HP, designed to support individuals with kidney failure. Additionally, it can complicate the administration of certain medications and dietary restrictions, such as a low-sodium diet. In pediatric patients, renal insufficiency can impact their nutritional requirements and necessitate adjustments in parenteral nutrition formulations.\n\nInsuficiencia renal can also be associated with other health issues, such as hyperuricemia and high triglyceride levels, which may further complicate treatment options. Overall, this serious condition requires careful medical intervention and monitoring to ensure that patients receive the appropriate nutritional support and manage their health effectively.", "PANCREATITIS AGUDA:\"PANCREATITIS AGUDA\" refers to acute pancreatitis, a medical condition characterized by sudden inflammation of the pancreas. This condition can lead to severe abdominal pain and requires immediate medical attention. It is often associated with complications such as hyperglycemia and can necessitate careful nutritional management, particularly in diabetic patients. \n\nAcute pancreatitis may require nutritional support, which can include enteral nutrition or parenteral nutrition, especially during the initial days of treatment. The severity of the condition can vary, being classified as mild, moderate, or severe, depending on the presence of complications and organ failure. Symptoms typically manifest between 24 to 36 hours after the peak production of cytokines, and the condition is marked by elevated levels of pancreatic enzymes such as amylase and lipase in the blood.\n\nAcute pancreatitis is a common reason for emergency consultations, with a presentation rate of 0.1% to 1.5% in large hospitals. It is crucial for patients experiencing this condition to receive intensive treatment and monitoring to manage the potential complications effectively.", "HEPATOPATÍAS:Hepatopathies refer to diseases affecting the liver, which can lead to nutritional alterations and complications. These liver diseases are significant enough to be considered a contraindication for the use of lorcaserin, a medication that may not be suitable for individuals with such conditions. Additionally, hepatopathies may necessitate specialized nutritional care to address the unique dietary needs and complications associated with liver dysfunction.", "SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO:**SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO (Short Bowel Syndrome)** is a medical condition characterized by a significant reduction in the absorptive capacity of the small intestine, often resulting from the surgical removal of a large portion of the intestine, congenital defects, or various medical conditions such as Crohn's disease and mesenteric ischemia. This condition leads to malabsorption of nutrients and can cause nutritional deficiencies, diarrhea, and other complications.\n\nPatients with SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO may require specialized nutritional management, including enteral nutrition or parenteral nutrition (NPT), particularly when there is a substantial loss of intestinal length. The condition can necessitate long-term nutritional support due to the reduced ability to absorb essential nutrients, making it a significant concern in clinical settings. In fact, SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO is one of the most frequent indications for NPT, accounting for approximately 32.2% of cases.\n\nOverall, SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO is a complex condition that requires careful management to address the challenges of nutrient absorption and to prevent complications associated with malnutrition."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}